WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.040
Turn a square four times and you might expect

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.290
four different pictures.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.230
But a pattern with its own symmetry repeats sooner.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.260
A completely symmetrical pattern looks the same

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.470
after every turn.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.050
So you cannot always divide by four.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.480
Dividing a total by the number of turns is tempting

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.590
and often wrong.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.660
It only works when every pattern has been counted the

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.910
same number of times.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:27.350
Each of the four small squares in a two by two tile is

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.360
black or white.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.100
Fixed on the page there are sixteen colourings.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.230
How many different tiles are there if the tile is

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:34.980
free to turn?

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.260
Pause, and resist dividing sixteen by four.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.430
Sort the sixteen by how many squares are black.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.450
None black: one colouring.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.910
One black: four.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.190
Two black: six.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.550
Three black: four.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:51.910
All black: one.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:53.420
Now turn them.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:54.880
No black is one tile.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:58.000
The four with one black square are all the same tile.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:01.080
The six with two black squares make two tiles:

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.080
four are side by side, and two are diagonal.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:07.680
Three black gives one tile, and all black gives one.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:09.680
That is six tiles altogether.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:14.650
Look at the group sizes: one, four, four, two,

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:15.890
four and one.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.370
They are not all four.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.210
The symmetrical tiles were counted fewer times,

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.540
which is exactly why sixteen divided by four gives

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:24.470
the wrong answer.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.750
When does dividing by the number of turns work?

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.290
When every turn gives a different position.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.870
Seat five different people round a table,

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.830
keeping clockwise order when you rotate the table.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.730
There are one hundred and twenty orders in a line.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.840
Each circular seating appears exactly five times as you

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.370
choose a place to start reading.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.930
One hundred and twenty divided by five is twenty-four.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.170
Divide only when every arrangement is repeated the same

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.160
number of times.

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:56.290
Otherwise, sort the arrangements into groups and

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.120
count the groups.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.770
Notebook challenge: in how many ways can four different

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:04.030
people sit round a circular table, if turning the whole

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:05.900
table does not count as different?
